# Backend workflow

Read app/main.tsr before changing routes, shared state or middleware. The greeting
is public; sensitive routes require application-owned authorization with app.use.
app/lib holds reusable logic; app/tests holds backend tests. JSON configuration
selects build paths, not public endpoints, middleware or client contracts.

Run tsrust check, tsrust test and tsrust format --check for backend changes.
Generate independent TypeScript or Rust clients with tsrust api generate --out.
The contract comes from checked Router source. Preserve owner edits and existing
clients; regenerate after route or response changes. Do not hand-edit generated
response codecs to bypass validation. Use tsrust dev for backend development.
Bring your own UI and call the HTTP API. No frontend package manager is required.
Do not publish, deploy or change signing trust without explicit authorization.
